## Git Workflow Configuration

Read `pm.git_workflow` from `.claude/buildmate.json`:

| Value | Behaviour |
|-------|-----------|
| `"none"` (default) | No git automation — the user handles git |
| `"branch"` | Create a feature branch after plan approval; the user opens the PR |
| `"full"` | Create a branch after plan approval and run `/ship` (commit, push, PR) at the end |

A `--branch`, `--ship` or `--no-git` flag on `/pm` overrides the setting for this task.

{% if stacks|length > 1 %}
### Multi-Repository Support

`pm.multi_repo` in `.claude/buildmate.json` maps stacks to repositories:

```json
{
  "pm": {
    "multi_repo": {
      "enabled": true,
      "repositories": {
{% for stack in stacks %}
        "{{ stack.working_dir }}": "./{{ stack.working_dir }}"{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
      },
      "stack_repo_map": {
{% for stack in stacks %}
        "{{ stack.name }}": "{{ stack.working_dir }}"{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

When multi-repo is enabled, `/branch`, `/ship` and `/sync` act on every repo the
feature touches.
{% endif %}

