## Phase 1: Planning (interactive)

Ask clarifying questions (AskUserQuestion) when requirements are ambiguous, the
scope is unclear, or several approaches are valid. Once the user approves the
plan, Phases 2–5 run without further questions.

{% if dashboard %}
```
task = dashboard_register_task(title="<task title from user request>", description="<description>")
dashboard_update_phase(task_id=task.id, phase="planning")
```
{% endif %}

### 1.1 Pick up previous context

If the session started with saved context (from the SessionStart hook) or the
request continues earlier work, read `.claude/context/features/*.md` for an
in-progress feature file and continue it instead of starting over.

### 1.2 Understand the request

- Read the request carefully
{% if stacks|length > 1 %}
- Decide which stacks are involved ({{ stacks|map(attribute='name')|join(', ') }})
{% endif %}
- Look at the existing code with Grep and Glob
- Read the relevant pattern and style files:
{% for stack in stacks %}
  - {{ stack.display_name }}:{% for pattern in stack.patterns %} `.claude/patterns/{{ pattern | installed(stack) }}`{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% for style in stack.styles %}, `.claude/styles/{{ style | installed(stack) }}`{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}

### 1.3 Create a feature file

Write `.claude/context/features/<feature-slug>.md`:

```markdown
# Feature: <Feature Name>

## Status: PLANNING
<!-- PLANNING | IN_PROGRESS | TESTING | IN_REVIEW | COMPLETE | BLOCKED -->

## Overview
<What this feature does and why>

## Requirements
- [ ] <Requirement 1>
- [ ] <Requirement 2>

## Technical Approach
{% for stack in stacks %}
### {{ stack.display_name }}
- Components: <what to build>
- Files: <which files>
{% endfor %}
{% if stacks|length > 1 %}

## API Contract
Agree on the contract before implementation so stacks can work in parallel:
GET /api/v1/resource -> { data: [...], meta: { page, total } }
POST /api/v1/resource -> { id, ...fields }
{% endif %}

## Tasks
| # | Task | Agent | Status |
|---|------|-------|--------|
| 1 | <task> | <agent> | PENDING |

## Completion Criteria
- [ ] All requirements implemented
- [ ] Tests written and passing
- [ ] Quality gates pass
- [ ] Code review approved
```

Also track the tasks in your task-list tool so the user can follow progress.

### 1.4 Get the plan approved

{% if dashboard %}
**You MUST call `dashboard_ask_question` and wait for approval** (do not use AskUserQuestion here):

```
result = dashboard_ask_question(
    task_id="<root_task_id>",
    question="Please review the plan above. Approve to proceed or provide feedback.",
    question_type="plan_review",
    options=["Approve", "Needs changes"],
    context="<feature file content or plan summary>",
    agent="orchestrator"
)
# "Approve" -> Phase 2; anything else -> revise the plan and ask again
```
{% else %}
Show the plan (the feature file) and ask for approval. For a trivial change you
may proceed without explicit approval, and say so.
{% endif %}

### 1.5 Git setup

If `pm.git_workflow` is `"branch"` or `"full"` (or `--branch`/`--ship` was
given): run `/branch <feature-slug>` and note the branch in the feature file.
If `/branch` fails (uncommitted changes, branch exists), tell the user and let
them resolve it.

{% if dashboard %}
### 1.6 Create all pipeline subtasks (dashboard)

Right after approval, create every subtask in `pending` status so the dashboard
shows the full pipeline:

```
{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set dev_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('developer') %}
{% if dev_agent %}
impl_subtask_{{ stack.name }} = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Implement {{ stack.display_name }} features", assigned_agent="{{ dev_agent.name }}")
{% endif %}
{% if stack | verifier %}
verify_subtask_{{ stack.name }} = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Verify {{ stack.display_name }}", assigned_agent="{{ stack | verifier }}")
{% endif %}
{% set test_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('tester') %}
{% if test_agent %}
test_subtask_{{ stack.name }} = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Write and run {{ stack.display_name }} tests", assigned_agent="{{ test_agent.name }}")
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
grind_subtask = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Run quality gates and fix failures", assigned_agent="grind")
{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set review_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('reviewer') %}
{% if review_agent %}
review_subtask_{{ stack.name }} = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Code review for {{ stack.display_name }}", assigned_agent="{{ review_agent.name }}")
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
eval_subtask = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Evaluate implementation quality", assigned_agent="eval-agent")
docs_subtask = dashboard_create_subtask(parent_id="<root_task_id>", title="Generate documentation", assigned_agent="documentation-specialist")
```

Every subtask goes `in_progress` before its delegation and `completed` or
`failed` (with a result) after it. A phase you skip is still marked
`completed` with `result="Skipped: <reason>"`.
{% endif %}

