## Phases 2–5: Autonomous Execution

From here the pipeline runs without asking the user. Stop and report only if:

- a verifier still fails after its retries,
- the grind agent does not converge,
- a reviewer returns BLOCKED, or review still asks for changes after 2 fix rounds,
- an infrastructure failure blocks progress.

**Delegate all implementation, testing and review.** You coordinate; you do not
write the code or the tests yourself.

---

## Phase 2: Implementation

Set the feature file status to `IN_PROGRESS`.
{% if dashboard %}
`dashboard_update_phase(task_id="<root_task_id>", phase="implementation")`
{% endif %}

{% if stacks|length > 1 %}
When the API contract is agreed, delegate the stacks **in parallel** (several
Agent calls in one message). When one stack depends on the other's output,
delegate them in sequence.

{% endif %}
{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set dev_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('developer') %}
{% if dev_agent %}
### {{ stack.display_name }}

```
Agent(subagent_type: "{{ dev_agent.name }}", description: "Implement {{ stack.name }} part", prompt: """
Implement: <specific task>
{% if stack.working_dir != "." %}
Working directory: {{ stack.working_dir }}
{% endif %}
Feature file: .claude/context/features/<feature-slug>.md
Requirements: <the relevant requirements>
{% if stacks|length > 1 %}
API contract: <the agreed contract>
{% endif %}
Report the files you changed and anything left open.
""")
```

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
After each delegation: read the report, check the changed files, update the
feature file and your task list.
{% if dashboard %}
Before each delegation: `dashboard_update_status(task_id=<subtask_id>, status="in_progress")`.
After it: `dashboard_update_status(task_id=<subtask_id>, status="completed" or "failed", result="<summary>")`.
{% endif %}

### 2.1 Verification

{% set ns_verify = namespace(any=false) %}
{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set verifier = stack | verifier %}
{% if verifier %}
{% set ns_verify.any = true %}
{% set dev = stack | dev_server %}
#### {{ stack.display_name }}

```
Agent(subagent_type: "{{ verifier }}", description: "Verify {{ stack.name }} changes", prompt: """
Verify what was just implemented:
<endpoints / pages / screens and the expected behaviour>
{% if dev.command %}
Dev server: `{{ dev.command }}` in `{{ stack.working_dir }}`, port {{ dev.port }}{% if dev.health_check %}, health check {{ dev.health_check }}{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
Follow the Dev Server rules in your instructions: reuse a running server, and
stop only servers you started. Fix failures and retry, at most 3 times.
Write your report to .agent-pipeline/{{ verifier }}-{{ stack.name }}.md.
Return VERIFIED or FAILED with details.
""")
```

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if not ns_verify.any %}
These stacks have no verifier agent; rely on the tests and quality gates in Phase 3.
{% else %}
- VERIFIED: continue to Phase 3.
- FAILED after retries: stop and report to the user.

Verifiers record the dev servers they start in `.agent-pipeline/dev-server.pids`
and stop them. If that file still exists afterwards, stop those processes:

```bash
[ -f .agent-pipeline/dev-server.pids ] && { xargs kill < .agent-pipeline/dev-server.pids 2>/dev/null; rm -f .agent-pipeline/dev-server.pids; }
```

Never kill processes by port: that would stop servers the user started.
{% if dashboard %}

Then register the verification artifacts yourself (Glob for files that exist):
`dashboard_add_artifact(task_id=<verify_subtask_id>, file_path=".agent-pipeline/<report>.md", artifact_type="markdown_report", label="Verification Report")`,
and for each screenshot in `.agent-pipeline/screenshots/*.png`:
`dashboard_add_artifact(task_id=<verify_subtask_id>, file_path="<png path>", artifact_type="screenshot", label="<name>")`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

