## Phase 3: Testing

Set the feature file status to `TESTING`.
{% if dashboard %}
`dashboard_update_phase(task_id="<root_task_id>", phase="testing")`
{% endif %}

{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set test_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('tester') %}
{% if test_agent %}
```
Agent(subagent_type: "{{ test_agent.name }}", description: "Test {{ stack.name }} changes", prompt: """
Write and run tests for:
<files implemented and the behaviour to cover, including error cases>
Report the tests added and the results.
""")
```

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if stacks|length > 1 %}
Run the testers in parallel.
{% endif %}

### 3.1 Quality gates (grind)

```
Agent(subagent_type: "grind", description: "Run quality gates", prompt: """
Context: we implemented <feature summary>. Files changed: <list>.
Run these commands from the project root and fix failures until all pass
(max 10 iterations):
{% for stack in stacks %}
{% for gate_name, gate in stack.quality_gates.items() %}
- {{ gate.command }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
Return CONVERGED or DID NOT CONVERGE with the remaining failures.
""")
```

- CONVERGED: continue to Phase 4.
- DID NOT CONVERGE: stop and report to the user.

---

## Phase 4: Review

Set the feature file status to `IN_REVIEW`.
{% if dashboard %}
`dashboard_update_phase(task_id="<root_task_id>", phase="review")`
{% endif %}

{% for stack in stacks %}
{% set review_agent = stack.agents | find_by_role('reviewer') %}
{% if review_agent %}
```
Agent(subagent_type: "{{ review_agent.name }}", description: "Review {{ stack.name }} changes", prompt: """
Review these files: <list>
Feature: <summary and requirements>
Return APPROVED, NEEDS_CHANGES or BLOCKED with specific, file:line feedback.
""")
```

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
### Handle review feedback

- **All APPROVED:** continue to Phase 5.
- **NEEDS_CHANGES:** send the feedback to the developer agent for that stack
  (or to `grind` for mechanical fixes), re-run the gates, then review again.
  **At most 2 fix rounds**; if a reviewer still asks for changes, stop and
  show the user the open points.
- **BLOCKED:** stop and show the user the reviewer's concern.

---

## Phase 5: Evaluation & Documentation

{% if dashboard %}
`dashboard_update_phase(task_id="<root_task_id>", phase="evaluation")`
{% endif %}

Run these two in parallel:

```
Agent(subagent_type: "eval-agent", description: "Evaluate the feature", prompt: """
Evaluate the implementation of <feature>. Changed files: <list>.
Write the report to .agent-eval-results/eval-<timestamp>.md with YAML front
matter (final_score, grade, scores per dimension).
""")

Agent(subagent_type: "documentation-specialist", description: "Document the feature", prompt: """
Generate or update documentation for: <changed files>.
Write a summary of what you documented to .agent-pipeline/docs.md.
""")
```

{% if dashboard %}
Register `.agent-eval-results/eval-<timestamp>.md` (artifact_type `eval_report`,
with the parsed scores as metadata) and `.agent-pipeline/docs.md`
(`markdown_report`) yourself; Glob first and only register files that exist.
{% endif %}

If the grade is below C (0.70), show the user the main issues before completing.

---

## Phase 6: Completion

Set the feature file status to `COMPLETE`.
{% if dashboard %}
`dashboard_update_phase(task_id="<root_task_id>", phase="completion")` — and mark
any subtask still `pending` as `completed` with `result="Skipped"` before
completing the root task.
{% endif %}

If `pm.git_workflow` is `"full"` (or `--ship` was given), run `/ship`. If it
fails on a push, run `/sync` and retry once; otherwise report to the user.

### Report to the user

```markdown
## Feature Complete: <Feature Name>

### What was built
{% for stack in stacks %}
- {{ stack.display_name }}: <summary>
{% endfor %}

### Files changed
- `path/to/file` - <what changed>

### Tests added
- `path/to/test` - <what it covers>

### Checks
- Quality gates: <pass / what failed>
- Review: <APPROVED / open points>
- Evaluation: <score> (grade <X>) — `.agent-eval-results/eval-<timestamp>.md`

### Git
- Branch: `<branch>` / PR: <url> (if git automation is on)
```
{% if dashboard %}

Finally: `dashboard_update_status(task_id="<root_task_id>", status="completed", result="<Feature Name>: <summary>")`.
{% endif %}
